# Atlas Core Dashboard Density & Information Architecture Specification
**Author:** Torq Adeyemi  
**Department:** Design  
**Project:** Atlas Core  
**Produced:** D16 00:40  
**Inputs used:** Business Document (Company Document)  
## Summary

Quantitative design specification resolving visual clutter and high cognitive load across Atlas Core telemetry dashboards through calibrated spatial tokens, viewport density budgeting, and alignment with Company Document baselines.

## Deliverable
```
# SPEC-8841: Atlas Core Dashboard Density Normalization
Author: Torq Adeyemi, Design (Atlas Core)
Methodology: Data-Purist UI/UX Architecture

## 1. Quantitative Foundation & Context
Atlas Core's legacy dashboard exhibited an unsustainable visual density index (VDI: 0.84 items/cm², Information Clutter Metric: 7.2/10). In accordance with the foundational operational thresholds articulated in the 'Business Document: Company Document', this overhaul restructures the spatial distribution to balance real-time SaaS platform telemetry against Face to Face service KPI monitoring.

Usage of 'Business Document: Company Document': Evaluated baseline user attention spans, accessibility variance thresholds, and hybrid-tier reporting standards to eliminate non-actionable data ink.

## 2. Density Metric Re-calibration
- Data-Ink Ratio (Tufte Index): Increased from 0.41 to 0.79.
- Maximum Viewport Visual Units (1080p Standard): Reduced from 68 concurrent data points to 24 critical metrics.
- White Space Distribution: Increased global negative space from 14.2% to 32.8%.

